                                        "entry_id": "f3c5e052-5ad1-3a6a-b773-301e877f70ba",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showing the previous location of geological features, correcting for any intervening crustal movements."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e4d4bc6-3294-4950-ba59-f276bba40408",
                                                "sense_id": "6357f051-488c-3f27-bcf4-283e76a0a77c",
                                                "text": "To improve the accuracy of spatial reconstruction through time, it is necessary to estimate and restore bulk strain by working backward in time so that the maps represent palinspastic reconstructions of geologic development."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b7d4be7-7ba2-4178-b3f0-026981dfc352",
                                                "sense_id": "6357f051-488c-3f27-bcf4-283e76a0a77c",
                                                "text": "Exactly when the first palinspastic reconstruction was published is uncertain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "231ac336-1045-4ae5-adef-58b4bb4ffbb7",
                                                "sense_id": "6357f051-488c-3f27-bcf4-283e76a0a77c",
                                                "text": "2009, K. Ustaszewski, et al., A map-view restoration of Alpine-Carpathian-Dinaridic system for the early Miocene, Nikolaus Froitzheim, Stefan M. Schmid (editors), Orogenic Processes in the Alpine Collision Zone, Swiss Journal of Geosciences Supplementary Issue, page S276,\nAnother set of palinspastic restorations aimed at restoring tectonic units based on the quantification of shortening amounts derived from balanced cross sections or from restoring offsets along major strike-slip faults."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
